items.good:
The tests hold, from the README and AC1, AC3 and AC4:
- the Example's exact listing;
- every ending in the table;
- capitals in an ending;
- no ending;
- hidden files and both kinds of running download;
- '.part' that is not the last ending;
- a taken name;
- ~/Downloads when no folder is named;
- nothing changed, the record's place included;
- each stop.
EXAMPLE_FILES now holds Projects/plan.txt, a folder whose name is no kind, so README line 52 is held for any folder. I ran them on Python 3.9 against a fresh reference tool and changed copies of it. They passed unchanged, and failed on each fault:
- endings not lowered (1 failure);
- '.part' matched anywhere in a name (1);
- the state folder written by a preview (2);
- a stop by `SystemExit()` (2);
- folders skipped only where their name is a kind (2).
Line and branch coverage and mutation testing are counted once the tool exists, at T3 action 3 and T5.
